<title>GERMANY: Vereinsbank current yr business &quot;excellent&quot;.</title>
<headline>Vereinsbank current yr business &quot;excellent&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayerische Vereinsbank AG chairman Albrecht Schmidt said on Thursday business in the first two months of the year so far had been &quot;excellent&quot;.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news briefing on its 1996 results, he added that interest and commission income had gone very well in the period and that spending was according to plan.</p>
<p>Income from own-account trading had also gone well as had risk provisions, in that there had been &quot;no major need&quot; for allocations in the period, Schmidt said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
